From a21cd78ea50c0a32d1ea0134aa38c59211a75b14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Boring Crocodile <crocodile@heilig.org>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 19:32:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat: allow to configure a subfolder count property for exact
 expand arrows

At the last loaded level of the folder tree every folder gets an
optimistic expand arrow, also folders without subfolders. The new
roundav_folder_count_property setting names a WebDAV property holding a
folder's number of subfolders (Nextcloud:
{http://nextcloud.org/ns}contained-folder-count). When set, the listing
asks for it in the same PROPFIND, and a folder with none shows no arrow.
Unset (default), the listing is unchanged.

On servers that report the property, this makes roundav_tree_depth = 1
(one request per opened folder) look exactly like the full tree.

Prepared by an AI agent (Claude, Anthropic); reviewed by Wald.
---
 config.inc.php.dist          |  8 +++++
 lib/PatchedWebDAVAdapter.php | 57 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 lib/roundav_files_engine.php | 58 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 3 files changed, 112 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/config.inc.php.dist b/config.inc.php.dist
index 1d5f422..43814fe 100644
--- a/config.inc.php.dist
+++ b/config.inc.php.dist
@@ -50,3 +50,11 @@ $config['roundav_search_threads'] = 1;
 
 // Folder levels the folder tree loads per request (default 2).
 $config['roundav_tree_depth'] = 2;
+
+// WebDAV property holding a folder's number of subfolders, asked for in the same PROPFIND
+// as the folder listing: a folder of the last loaded level without subfolders then shows
+// no expand arrow. null (default): not asked; every folder of the last loaded level gets
+// an arrow until it is opened.
+$config['roundav_folder_count_property'] = null;
+// Nextcloud:
+// $config['roundav_folder_count_property'] = '{http://nextcloud.org/ns}contained-folder-count';
